  "interpretation": "M1 substantially outperforms M0 across all criteria (level RMSE, LOOCV RMSE, AIC, BIC), confirming that a spending-to-outcome lag exists. M2 shows marginal improvement over M1 in level RMSE (0.434 vs 0.441) and LOOCV RMSE (0.469 vs 0.472), but the advantage is small and does not survive BIC penalization (M2 wins in only 41% of countries by BIC). The tempo drift mu_H1 = +0.15 yr/yr should therefore be interpreted as suggestive rather than definitive. The robust finding is the existence of a lag (M1 vs M0), not its time-variation (M2 vs M1)."
